obvious like marching  band why would there be a marching band  like in a [ __ ] airport playing yankee  doodle deity of all things of course  there never would be but i just think  that was like kind of funny but so this  the humor is kind of like that it's kind  of just like the little subtle kind of  touches which i actually really  appreciated now interest another thing  that's interesting about this is that  the kills actually start out kind of  slow like i said he kills valerie first  but they don't even show that until  later and even though the sequence where  she gets killed is really stylish it's  not all that gruesome i mean she does  get her hand like kind of torn off and  that's kind of gross but it's not like  super over the top  but the movie gets a lot more violent  and a lot more like disgusting like as  time goes on which actually kind of  surprised me but like in a good way uh  the special effects work for considering  what the budget probably was is actually  quite good a couple victims get beheaded  and you know the guy like carries the  heads around and does all kind of crazy  [ __ ] with them like putting them on  turntables and stuff um the bodies get  like pierced with  vinyl records like 45s um and actually  what is a really good scene like them  sticking in there it actually looks  really realistic um there's a great  scene toward the end where there's like  this big uh you know he he's kind of  like in a car and he's trying to like  hit all the people like in the funeral  like are some of the victims that he  killed and he hits one car and like one  of the bodies like comes flying out of  the coffin and the head had been taken  off and so obviously it was sewn back on  so it's kind of like hanging off like  that and that was like actually really  really good so you know and the car  crash actually looked looked realistic  there's a point where someone falls off  a building and makes like a really nasty  mess on the street below so this does it  doesn't start out with like a lot of  violence or gore or something like that  but it kind of like more than makes up  for it toward the end like it gets  really really gory like toward the end  which i really liked so  you know while disco path it's not  strictly a giallo because it's not  really a murder mystery i mean there's  no mystery about who the killer is it's  obviously dwayne i mean they don't make  any secret about that um but it does  have enough gloss touches to maybe kind  of endear it to fans of the genre like  the look of it the style of it um the  retro vibe of it i think that's more  in keeping with giallo rather than it  having like a lot of the plot points  around it like i said with the mass  killer and all that kind of stuff so you  know keep that in mind um and also if  you really like or if you'd really like  to see a pretty well done homage to  uh you know kind of the slashers of  yesteryear then you'll probably dig this  as well as i mentioned the tone is a  little bit uneven um you know some of  the characters seem like they're sort of  aware that they're in a comedy and the  other ones are like playing it straight  so it's a little bit odd um there are a  few parts of it that you know that don't  really work or there's a couple things  in there that i kind of wish had been  explored more but they weren't because  the movie isn't really that long it's  only like 85 minutes but i mean those  are pretty minor minor quibbles i  thought this was like a pretty enjoyable  movie overall like it has a really cool  look to it um you know so i thought it  was pretty nifty also um i have to give  a big shout out to  the score and like all the music that  was used there's some casey and the  sunshine band in there there's a boy  from new york city that song i can't  remember who does it and like i said  flight 76 so there's like a lot of  really cool like disco music in it that  you will recognize so i really like that  as well i heard i don't know if this  ever happened or not but i heard that  the writer director was going to  put out a soundtrack album like on vinyl  for this movie which would actually like  be pretty rad because like i said  there's a lot of really good disco tunes  in this so yeah if you like disco if you  like 70s era slashers if you like giallo  films and want to see something that's a  little bit like a giallo film but not  exactly then this would be a really  really good one to check out and like i  said it's available for free on to be at  the moment so that will do it for this  flickers of fear again continuing on  with giallo july and i will see you guys  on the next one  bye
 

